+# Scoped canonical review — initial source
+
+Read complete note6149eb04, primarya226b176, static30ba9a75, mobileb7ed5c1c, declared dictionary premise/full-carrier/gated-ring/low-charge sections, and isolated/mutation evidence. Exact read identities are in READ_HASHES.json. This reviewer authored the earlier mobile four-choice proof: that portion is canonical-port confirmation, not a new independent review of my own mathematics. The static argument had a separate earlier conceptual review; this pass checks consolidation, quantified domain and nonuniform Jp extension.
+
+Mathematical PASS for the stated original bounds. A connected finite balanced directed graph is strongly connected by the source-SCC argument; after contracting SCCs total inflow equals outflow at each component, and a source with zero inflow has zero outflow. Every ordered pair therefore has a simple directed path. Each prefix creates only its two endpoint charges; this is support existence over unrestricted winding sectors, not hopping preparation. Native phases are removed only by the explicit unitary dictionary, not discarded in the original basis.
+
+Each Fp(I-Sp) has eigenvalues zero and two on the alternating pair and zero elsewhere. With arbitrary Jp>=0, positivity and the same componentwise uniform dictionary-basis kernel persist term by term, including Jp=0. Thus the added nonuniform extension needs no translation invariance or stronger graph theorem. Static pair energy is exactly2U. The mobile row bound counts each undirected edge once at its charged source; degree4 occupied or degree2 with4 vacancies gives at most4D, and absolute Hermitian row sums control phases without cancellation. D conservation, ice annihilation and neutral total signed charge give the stated charged lower bound. The fixed-position trial has zero hopping expectation but is not a mobile eigenstate. No neutral spectral gap, mobility, nonconfinement or winding-specific support follows.
+
+Finite helpers support the general arguments honestly: static all-pair fixtures are not an ice census; mobile repeated depth neighborhoods are not a D2 spectrum. The negative-J, undercounted capacity, reverse-phase and path-sign controls discriminate their stated local errors. The primary executes both helpers and binds its provisional dictionary and note. Isolated evidence matches that declared closure; no additional scientific runtime import appears.
+
+One execution-contract defect was reported to root: mobile helper unconditionally resets signal.alarm(180) when invoked through runpy, extending the primary's absolute deadline after static work. The final elapsed guard detects eventual excess but does not enforce interruption at the initial deadline. Guard the helper alarm for standalone execution or use remaining time. Root accepted this repair. No source edit was made by this reviewer.
+
+Final canonical disposition is held pending that repair and the separately proposed stronger D2 variational bound. This review does not cover an unreviewed new upper bound. No full pipeline, formal audit or authority verdict was issued.
